00042:     "3_independent_producer_caller_receiver_reconstruction": {
00043:       "index_domain": "Battler.pokemonIndex is bound from idxParty by pbInitPokemon; participants is its own accessor array. Battle/Battler side predicates compare parity. pbUpdateParticipants rejects self fainted or player-side, then appends each living opposing battler's partyindex only if absent. These are player-side party indices on live foe records, not global seats or Battler objects.",
00044:       "initial_entry": "Complete StartBattleCore creates sides/AI/scene/send-out and weather/terrain presentation before calling OnAllBattlersEnteringBattle, then BattleLoop. OnAll calculates priority and forwards initial live indices to OnBattlerEnteringBattle. For each entrant that survived the initial gate, first calls RecordBattlerAsParticipated, which sets applicable money flag then updates all living battlers. This precedes entry message, healing positions, hazards, forms/abilities/items and the first ordinary attack.",
00045:       "replacement": "Ordinary stored SwitchOut executor may be stopped by Pursuit/decision; otherwise recall/leave/lineup/message and replacement initialization/order/send-out happen before OnBattlerEnteringBattle. Outgoing cleanup is not itself the direct update call. New entry causes the positive record append; already recorded old members remain historical entries.",
00046:       "receiver": "GainExp first may request wild-success presentation, then returns for noninternal/expGain-off. It scans opposing nonempty recorded objects only when fainted/captured, counts currently able owned participants, calls EV before EXP for eligible player-segment recipients and clears that processed array only after normal processing. ExpShare/ExpAll and ownership remain their exact gates. Complete Reset clears participants only after its earlier HP/reference/effect-reset prefix is reached normally.",
00047:       "finite_negative": "Own rg86a31d found ordinary direct updater in Record and an Arena initial-entry override. Ordinary nonvariant premise excludes Arena. No direct-update search is promoted to proof attacks or plugins never cause participation updates: an attack may indirectly trigger replacement/entry effects. The positive before-attack entry path suffices here."
00048:     },
00049:     "4_normal_control_failure_sensitive_observation": {
00050:       "premise": "Ordinary valid internal1v1, living player P0 with legal living reserve P1, living foe W; unique partyindices0/1; ordinary successful startup/entry, no plugin or participation mutation, no interfering entry effect. Growth enabled; P1 remains able and player-owned at later growth. No exact damage/EXP arithmetic or native execution claimed.",
00051:       "trace": [
00052:         "Initial entry records W.participants=[0] before anyone attacks or receives an attack.",
00053:         "During a legal P0→P1 replacement, a failure before new entry does not establish registration of1. Normal new entry records W.participants=[0,1] before P1 attacks or is hit.",
00054:         "A later ordinary non-damaging action followed by existing poison fainting W can reach growth; the recorded P1 is considered under current able/ownership gates despite no prior P1 damage exchange. This is already derived from WP41 registration plus WP42 receiver.",
00055:         "Entry hazard can instead faint P1 after its index was appended; later current-able filter can exclude it. Being recorded does not guarantee EXP/EV or survival.",
00056:         "An ordinary later attack between already resident members need not change this unique set. No-array-delta alone cannot establish absence of a method invocation or an unmet behavior contract."
00057:       ],
00058:       "ordinary_control": "With only initial P0 and no replacement, history remains0 until a reached reset/processed growth clear or other separately specified mutation. Source and detailed contract predict the same set at the meaningful growth boundary.",
00059:       "evidence_level": "STATIC_SOURCE + COMPLETE_CONTEXT + DERIVED_VECTOR; NOT_EXECUTED"
00060:     },
00061:     "5_strongest_required_argument_and_counter_resolution": {
00062:       "strongest_required": [
00063:         "WP39 positively says lists are registered at 被攻击/被换出等更新点. Nonexclusive 等 permits more triggers, but does not by itself make inaccurate positive examples true.",
00064:         "A synopsis is still normative text. A reader could build attack/withdraw-only bookkeeping and miss no-attack entry or hazard-time participation, and a correct paragraph in another file does not automatically cure every contradiction.",
00065:         "Timing before hazards matters when entry immediately faints or a later callback fails. Therefore replacing just those examples with entry notification could be a bounded P3 clarification, preserving all correct details."
00066:       ],
00067:       "independent_resolution": [
00068:         "The specified contract explicitly assigns switching/entry to WP41 and growth to WP42 in WP39 purpose/non-goals and cross-references. WP41§4.2 unambiguously requires participation registration first, then hazards; an attack-only implementation would violate that existing required rule already. No newly missing entry obligation is demonstrated.",
00069:         "WP39 line192 gives nonexclusive historical-record examples and does not say only on those events, after damage, or one method call for every attack. Its interface context does not fix an implementation callback placement. Redundant maintenance during an attack/withdraw can be behaviorally equivalent when the history is already populated at entry.",
00070:         "The proposed ordinary no-attack growth observation therefore agrees with the complete contract. We preserve its source truth without turning extra precision or default callee placement into a new required ticket.",
00071:         "This is a finite interpretation judgment, not a claim the examples are well chosen or that all future positive contradictions are excused. If root independently identifies a normal observable mismatch against the combined rules, that separate exact premise can change the result."
00072:       ],
00073:       "optional": "No new optional proposed merely to restate the already authoritative entry rule. Root may choose editorial cleanup later; none starts here."
00074:     },
00075:     "6_cancel_failure_partial_commit_and_save_boundaries": {
00076:       "cancel": "WP41 separates eligibility, UI cancel, registration and execution. Cancellation before a reached switch registration/executor does not call this new-entry chain; there is no new promise that every UI cancel restores unrelated earlier state. No UI was executed.",
00077:       "before_entry_failure": "Recall/leave/message/initialization/send-out can fail before Record. New Pokemon may already be bound or sent before entry notification; none of that alone proves the new index was appended to the foe. Original outgoing record is not retroactively removed by this reasoning.",
00078:       "after_entry_failure": "Money flag or an earlier foe's participant list may already change before a later updater/scene/hazard/ability exception. Entry registration is before hazards, so immediate faint does not undo that history. No transaction or automatic rollback is inferred.",
00079:       "growth_failure": "An EV/EXP/message failure may occur after earlier recipients were changed but before participants=[]; no idempotency or durable save is guaranteed. Noninternal/expGain-off early return precedes normal clear. Capture Reset effect-reset error can occur before participants clear after earlier HP/reference changes.",
00080:       "persistence": "These arrays are battle-local bookkeeping; no new save root is inferred. Persistent Pokemon EV/EXP/HP and later save/load belong distinct actual writers and already bounded KERNEL contracts. Native roundtrip, scene output and host behavior remain unobserved."
00081:     },
